    {
      "t": "h2",
      "text": "Three things\nthe review found"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Quoted from the full review. Each one carries its date, source and a fix inside."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "tag": "span",
      "cls": "n",
      "text": "01"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "“Tested, warranty” is in the title but nowhere in the listing"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "A buyer spending $3,500 on a pendant wants proof it works and to know what the warranty covers."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "tag": "span",
      "cls": "n",
      "text": "02"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "One robot family, seven spellings"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Technicians search the way the nameplate or the manual reads, and plenty type it without the hyphen. A listing shouldn't depend on the search engine guessing that “R-2000iB” and “R2000iB” are the same robot."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "tag": "span",
      "cls": "n",
      "text": "03"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "text": "Serial numbers use space that buyers’ search words should get"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Nobody searches a serial number before they know it exists. Meanwhile the words buyers do type — “industrial robot arm,” “Yaskawa” for Motoman, payload, application — are missing."
    },
